FAQ SECTION: Login and Account Access
Document Type: Draft for SME Review
Author: Knowledge Management Team
Last Edited: 2025-03-22

Q: How do I create a new account?
A: Visit the signup page at https://app.platform.example.com/signup. Enter your work email address, choose a password (min 12 chars, must include uppercase, lowercase, digit, and special character), and accept the Terms of Service. You will receive a verification email — click the link within 24 hours to activate your account. After activation, you can set up your organization profile and invite team members.

Q: Can I sign up using my Google or GitHub account?
A: Yes. On the signup page, click "Continue with Google" or "Continue with GitHub". You will be redirected to authenticate with the selected provider. On first login, you will be prompted to set up your organization profile. Note: SSO-managed organizations may restrict social login options.

Q: I can't log in after my company enforced SSO. What should I do?
A: When your organization enforces SSO, existing password-based accounts are linked to your SSO identity by email address. Log in using the "Sign in with SSO" button with your corporate credentials. If you encounter an error, your IT administrator may need to add your account to the SSO provisioning group. Contact your internal helpdesk for assistance.

Q: How do I manage multiple organization memberships?
A: If you belong to multiple organizations on the platform, you will see an organization switcher in the top-left corner of the dashboard after login. Click to switch between organizations. Each organization maintains separate settings, projects, and billing. You can be a member of up to 10 organizations with a single account.
